<title>USA: Southland Corp Q1 net rises slightly.</title>
<headline>Southland Corp Q1 net rises slightly.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Thousands, Except Per-Share Data)</p>
<p>			  (UNAUDITED)</p>
<p>							   Three Months</p>
<p>							   Ended March 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	   1996</p>
<p> Total revenues			     $1,626,023   $1,581,651</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>   Cost of goods sold			1,154,633    1,120,568</p>
<p>   Operating, selling, g&amp;a expenses	438,288	428,867</p>
<p>   Interest expense, net			23,899	 23,068</p>
<p>						   1,616,820    1,572,503</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes		  9,203	  9,148</p>
<p> Income taxes					3,681	  3,659</p>
<p> Net earnings					5,522	  5,489</p>
<p>Net earnings per common share</p>
<p>   (primary and fully diluted) (1)	     .01	    .01</p>
<p>Weighted average primary and fully</p>
<p>  diluted shares				 409,923	409,923</p>
<p> Operating stores at end of period	   5,409	  5,435</p>
<p>(1) Convertible quarterly income debt securities are common stock equivalents, and are not included in the first quarter primary earnings per share calculation because they have an antidilutive effect.</p>
<p>While the first quarter 1996 earnings per share calculation has been restated, this issue only affects the first quarter calculation and no other 1996 earnings per share calculations will require restatement.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
